{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778938062,"nonce":"7M3TvzLQDZG8SpqAFsZ/vGeiekU=","title":"Mandible canonical issue/work ledger with git-bug import/export","message":"## Problem\nMandible currently treats `git-bug` as the authoritative issue store. That has been useful for local-first issue tracking, but it limits typed metadata, deterministic querying, comment/work-unit modeling, and agent-oriented work records.\n\nMandible likely needs a central canonical issue/work ledger: issues, comments, status, priority, labels, relationships, repos, branches, commits, sessions, auth requests, handoffs, and provenance should be first-class structured records owned by Mandible. Markdown should remain the human body/comment format, not the whole data model.\n\n## Direction\nDesign and implement a Mandible-owned issue/work-item backend, likely SQLite plus an append-only event/history model, with typed entities and derived projections for UI/API queries.\n\nThe code repos should link to Mandible issue IDs through commit trailers, branch names, auth requests, comments, and related metadata, but the canonical issue state does not need to live inside each repo's code history.\n\n## Required import/export\n`git-bug` import/export should be supported by default. This is not optional migration polish: existing Mandible and project issues already live in `git-bug`, so Mandible needs a path to import them into the central ledger and, at least initially, export/sync back for compatibility.\n\nGit-Bug migration should preserve at minimum:\n- issue id / short id mapping\n- title and body\n- status\n- labels, including conventions such as `parent:\u003cid\u003e` and `merged`\n- comments\n- authors/timestamps where available\n- create/edit provenance\n- cross-links that Mandible already derives from labels or text\n\n## Future import/export\nGitHub Issues should probably be supported eventually, because it is a common public/project issue surface and may be needed for repos that already use GitHub-native issues.\n\nDo not assume support for other trackers at the start. Plane, Huly, Linear, Jira, OpenProject, Redmine, etc. can inform the model, but adapters for them should wait until there is a concrete need.\n\n## Design constraints\n- Keep Mandible's model specific to agentic coding/work orchestration rather than building a generic Linear clone.\n- Treat comments as first-class records, not just text appended to an issue body.\n- Treat relationships as typed data: parent/child, blocks, duplicate, related, fixed-by, caused-by, session/auth-request links.\n- Preserve append-only/audit-friendly history even when current state is mutable.\n- Provide stable IDs that are easy to reference from commits, branches, auth requests, and agent prompts.\n- Keep Markdown useful for human-readable descriptions and comments.\n- Make import/export repeatable and idempotent enough for migration tests.\n\n## Out of scope for the first implementation\n- Supporting every external tracker.\n- Replacing all existing Issues UI at once.\n- Public multi-user SaaS semantics beyond what Mandible needs locally.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}